# Theos, the iOS/tvOS tweak + application toolchain.
# https://theos.dev/docs/installation-linux
#
# roothide/theos's bin/install-theos is the entire install story and the only
# supported entry point -- it owns the dependency lists, the fakeroot
# alternative, the toolchain tarball URLs and the SDK fetch, all of which move
# independently of the docs. Run it and get out of its way.
#
# The two things it is given:
#
#   THEOS  -- unset, the installer picks a shell rc by hand and appends
#             `export THEOS=~/theos` to it. Every rc it would choose is managed
#             here, so the edit gets reverted by the next apply and re-appended
#             by the one after, forever. Exported, set_theos() is a no-op. The
#             durable half of the same setting is in .commonprofile.
#   CI     -- the installer asks, interactively, whether the toolchain should
#             support Swift. An apply is frequently not attached to a terminal,
#             and that `read` under the installer's own `set -e` fails on EOF
#             and takes the install with it. $CI is the installer's own escape
#             hatch for exactly this, and skipping that prompt is the only
#             thing it does here. It leaves `stoolchain` at whatever the
#             installer initialised it to, which upstream hardcodes to no.
#
# Two seds, each addressed at a single line of the installer.
#
# The first is a workaround for an upstream bug, not a preference. The debian
# branch's dependency line ends `... perl zip git libxml2`, and Ubuntu 26.04
# has no binary package by that name -- the runtime went to a versioned name
# when the soname bumped, leaving `libxml2` a virtual reference with no
# installation candidate. apt then refuses the whole transaction and the
# installer exits 3, which took down both Ubuntu legs of the image build while
# Fedora (where `libxml2` is still a real package) passed. libxml2-dev is the
# name that survives a soname bump, and 021-apt-packages already installs it,
# so this asks for nothing new. Addressed to the apt line alone: `libxml2` is
# correct on the arch, redhat and suse branches and must not be rewritten there.
#
# The second is the preference. We want Swift, and $CI on its own answers no,
# so this flips the default the prompt would have overwritten -- together they
# mean "don't ask, and yes". That gets the larger kabiroberai
# swift-toolchain-linux build in place of the smaller L1ghtmann iOSToolchain.
# For the non-Swift one, remove $THEOS/toolchain/linux/iphone and re-run this
# by hand without that sed. Anchored, so it misses the commented-out copy of
# the same line further down the installer.
export THEOS="$HOME/theos"
CI=1 bash -c "$(curl -fsSL https://github.com/roothide/theos/raw/refs/heads/master/bin/install-theos \
	| sed -e '/apt install -y build-essential/s/ libxml2/ libxml2-dev/' \
	      -e 's/^[[:space:]]*stoolchain="n"$/stoolchain="y"/')"
